     "result_text_tail": "you were unavailable:**\n- **Format:** a deep deck (about 45\u201350 slides, analysed as a problem) for the CEO to bring to the board, in the navy theme.\n- **Sizing:** the issue tree is cut by profit lever: gross margin, store costs, e-commerce. Every action is sized at FY2025 prices and volumes, with no sales growth.\n- **Fiscal years:** I read FY2026 as the first plan year, as the brief does. But if fiscal years end in January, FY2026 is mostly over by the February 2027 board meeting. That would make the $23M covenant estimate optimistic. The deck flags this, and the next steps ask the CFO to confirm with the lender which months the covenant covers.\n- **Three planning assumptions (not in the pack):**\n  - Sales are split equally across the four store-staffing groups.\n  - Half of the promotion reset lands in FY2026.\n  - The store-exit gain is split evenly by store, because the pack has no per-store figures.\n- **Not counted:** sales growth, vendor-funding recovery, a lower delivery rate and depreciation saved by the store exits are left out as upside.\n\n**Grades:** no numbers are left as placeholders. All 264 numbers come from one source, the pack, so none has a second source to corroborate it.\n\nPossible next steps are adding per-store EBITDA or markdown dollars to firm up the store-exit and vendor-funding numbers, or switching the theme.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- `harlow-margin-plan.pptx`\n- `harlow-margin-plan-sources.xlsx`\n- `harlow-margin-plan.json` (the spec, kept for edits)"
